        "title": "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector",
        "key_prerequisites": [
          {
            "topic_id": "1104",
            "name": "Unit Vectors",
            "href": "/topics/1104",
            "type": ""
          }
        ],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let <span class=\"math\">[MATH: [4; \u2212 5; 1]]</span> Find a unit vector that is parallel to <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\mathbf{a}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Let [MATH: [4; \u2212 5; 1]] Find a unit vector that is parallel to [MATH: \\mathbf{a}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|}]</span></p><p>Using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |a||= sqrt(a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}); = sqrt(4^{2} + (\u2212 5)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(16 + 25 + 1); = sqrt(42).]</span></p><p>Finally, we divide <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\mathbf{a}]</span> by its length and get the following unit vector:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: u|= (a)/(|a|); = (1)/(sqrt(42))a; = (1)/(sqrt(42)) \u22c5 [4; \u2212 5; 1]; = [4/sqrt(42); \u2212 5/sqrt(42); 1/sqrt(42)]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n[MATH: \\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|}]\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n[MATH: |a||= sqrt(a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}); = sqrt(4^{2} + (\u2212 5)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(16 + 25 + 1); = sqrt(42).]\n\nFinally, we divide [MATH: \\mathbf{a}] by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n[MATH: u|= (a)/(|a|); = (1)/(sqrt(42))a; = (1)/(sqrt(42)) \u22c5 [4; \u2212 5; 1]; = [4/sqrt(42); \u2212 5/sqrt(42); 1/sqrt(42)]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nLet [MATH: [4; \u2212 5; 1]] Find a unit vector that is parallel to [MATH: \\mathbf{a}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n[MATH: \\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|}]\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n[MATH: |a||= sqrt(a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}); = sqrt(4^{2} + (\u2212 5)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(16 + 25 + 1); = sqrt(42).]\n\nFinally, we divide [MATH: \\mathbf{a}] by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n[MATH: u|= (a)/(|a|); = (1)/(sqrt(42))a; = (1)/(sqrt(42)) \u22c5 [4; \u2212 5; 1]; = [4/sqrt(42); \u2212 5/sqrt(42); 1/sqrt(42)]]"
      },
