        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A(1,1,2)]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: B(2,-2,3).]</span> Find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |\\overrightarrow{AB}|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Let [MATH: A(1,1,2)] and [MATH: B(2,-2,3).] Find [MATH: |\\overrightarrow{AB}|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We have </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: OA^(\u2192) = a = i + j + 2k,; OB^(\u2192) = b = 2i \u2212 2j + 3k.]</span></p><p>Expressing <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\overrightarrow{AB}]</span> as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: AB^(\u2192)|= OB^(\u2192) \u2212 OA^(\u2192); = b \u2212 a; = (2i \u2212 2j + 3k) \u2212 (i + j + 2k); = i \u2212 3j + k.]</span></p><p>Now, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |AB^(\u2192)||= sqrt(1^{2} + (\u2212 3)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(1 + 9 + 1); = sqrt(11).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We have\n\n[MATH: OA^(\u2192) = a = i + j + 2k,; OB^(\u2192) = b = 2i \u2212 2j + 3k.]\n\nExpressing [MATH: \\overrightarrow{AB}] as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n[MATH: AB^(\u2192)|= OB^(\u2192) \u2212 OA^(\u2192); = b \u2212 a; = (2i \u2212 2j + 3k) \u2212 (i + j + 2k); = i \u2212 3j + k.]\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n[MATH: |AB^(\u2192)||= sqrt(1^{2} + (\u2212 3)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(1 + 9 + 1); = sqrt(11).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nLet [MATH: A(1,1,2)] and [MATH: B(2,-2,3).] Find [MATH: |\\overrightarrow{AB}|.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe have\n\n[MATH: OA^(\u2192) = a = i + j + 2k,; OB^(\u2192) = b = 2i \u2212 2j + 3k.]\n\nExpressing [MATH: \\overrightarrow{AB}] as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n[MATH: AB^(\u2192)|= OB^(\u2192) \u2212 OA^(\u2192); = b \u2212 a; = (2i \u2212 2j + 3k) \u2212 (i + j + 2k); = i \u2212 3j + k.]\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n[MATH: |AB^(\u2192)||= sqrt(1^{2} + (\u2212 3)^{2} + 1^{2}); = sqrt(1 + 9 + 1); = sqrt(11).]"
      },
